# Healthcare Penetration Testing Lab

## Project Overview

This project demonstrates the design and implementation of an isolated penetration testing laboratory using Oracle VirtualBox.

The environment simulates a healthcare organization's internal network and was built to safely perform ethical hacking activities, including reconnaissance, vulnerability assessment, exploitation, social engineering simulation, and network traffic analysis.

All testing was conducted in an isolated virtual environment to ensure that no external systems were affected.



## Objectives

- Build a secure and isolated penetration testing lab
- Simulate a healthcare network
- Perform host discovery and network reconnaissance
- Identify running services and potential vulnerabilities
- Demonstrate ethical exploitation techniques
- Analyse captured network traffic
- Provide security recommendations based on findings



## Technologies Used

| Technology                       | Purpose 
|------------                      |---------
| Oracle VirtualBox                | Virtualization Platform 
| Kali Linux                       | Attacker Machine 
| Ubuntu Server                    | Healthcare Server 
| Windows 7                        | Vulnerable Workstation 
| Metasploitable 2                 | Vulnerable Linux Machine 
| Nmap                             | Network Reconnaissance 
| Metasploit Framework             | Exploitation 
| Wireshark                        | Packet Analysis 
| Social Engineering Toolkit (SET) | Phishing Simulation 

